      "url": "https://github.com/kco994553-star/Investment-System1/commit/11d2f25ef8bef3459ca969f50eec190099f15ecb",
      "message": "[proposal] FPIA fix round 3 H1-H7 (CDR-014 §14): AC-32.spoof as a conservative over-approximation, environment-independent verdict, verifier hardening\n\nH1 identity: GitHub constant expressions in name/run-name are folded ('literal' with '' escapes,\nformat() over literals, nested); a non-foldable expression there is FOUND fail-closed (identity not\nstatically determinable). Identity keys = for s, NFKC(s), skeleton(s), skeleton(NFKC(s)),\nNFKC(skeleton(s)): casefold, delete everything but ASCII [a-z0-9]; a Track C name/stem key that is a\nSUBSTRING of a key of the workflow's name, run-name or filename stem is a claim. The ICU 74.2 table\nkeeps NFKC-unstable sources (1788 code points), fixing the round-2 NFKC-before-skeleton D1 bug.\n\nH2 what a complement workflow can run: the verdict no longer depends on resolving cd,\nworking-directory, shell flags, wrappers or quoting. Mention set M from R and A_V only (tool\nstems/basenames, Track C test module stems, Track C module dotted paths, A_V basenames, the Track C\nworkflow path); the workflow (decoded + folded, and raw without backslash-newline/quotes, ANSI-C\ndecoded) and every in-tree code/config file it can reach (any token naming a tree file, local action\ndirectories, reusable workflows, make/npm/yarn/pnpm/tox/nox configuration, python -m modules under any\nroot, pytest @argsfiles and -c ini files) are scanned; any mention, Track C import, glob over Track C\npaths (whole-suite globs are notes), path naming a Track C file, pytest -k/-m or exclusion selection\nkeeping Track C tests, or same-repository remote workflow/action is FOUND unless attributed as before.\nThe fix-round-2 resolver output is kept as evidence (resolver_reasons) and for the whole-suite note.\nThe running verifier's own files (byte-identical to it or to a version on its history) are\nself-placement, not scanned. Summary line names dynamic_invocation_detection NOT_CLAIMED (D3-c) and\nout_of_tree_code_analysis NOT_ANALYSED (D3-e) whenever their fields are non-empty.\n\nH3 work dir, TMPDIR and interpreter directory resolved once (realpath); plugin_findings compares\nrealpath to realpath; pytest's basetemp in FPIA's own child runs written as pytest-of-<user>.\nH4 --verify-output rejects duplicate JSON keys and non-basename side-file names, reads/writes UTF-8\nwhatever the locale, records/prints/checks run_sha256 (integrity, not authentication: D3-a); --out\nwhose directory is missing or not writable is refused before the audit; CI prints run_sha256.\nH5 fetch/ls-remote output split on LF (and CR) only; status-line regexes ASCII-whitespace only.\nH6 AC-04 counts every Track C-namespace path at T, including paths not in R.\nH7 runtime_provenance.verifier.files lists every file under tools/integration/ (incl. _vendor/**).\n\nTier 1 regressions in test_integration_fpia_fix3.py pin every round-2 variant (22 D1 + 41 D2 + S24V2\nFOUND; D3-c and D3-e pinned as current behaviour). Open user decisions D3-a..D3-e and the G7\ninterpretation are not decided.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019znshzTYgyBnuuBmSxdPFN"
    },
    {
      "id": "E013",
      "kind": "git_commit",
      "repository": "kco994553-star/Investment-System1",
      "ref": "babf0a41dd8a740190743ee1e27289b17d8118d3",
      "bytes": 4166,
      "sha256": "0b79722904507345eb697c2d0beea40cfb1e2c08eeb436cee38a6845ad865f1b",
      "url": "https://github.com/kco994553-star/Investment-System1/commit/babf0a41dd8a740190743ee1e27289b17d8118d3",
      "message": "[proposal] FPIA fix round 2 G1-G7/F2 (CDR-014 §14): YAML spoof identity, resolved workflow references, structural fetch status, --out refusal and verifier, path-independent result_sha256, AC-04 wording, PR scope\n\nFixes the verified findings of the fix-round verification of 465354a (v-real, v-adversarial,\ncompleteness). Every adversarial probe of that round is pinned as a Tier 1 regression with its\nexpected component/status (S0-S19, S21, S24, F1-E5, F4 reuse). Open user decisions are kept as\ncurrent behaviour and recorded, not decided: D3-a verifier authentication in CI, D3-b a\ncontent-independent job-id collision rule (collision stays a note, S17), D3-c dynamically\nconstructed invocations (NOT_CLAIMED, S15/S16), D3-d #28 attribution.\n\nG1 (AC-32.spoof identity): complement workflows are read with PyYAML (safe_load validity gate,\ncompose with the pure-Python SafeLoader); the workflow name/run-name and filename stem are\ncompared with the Track C workflow's name and stem after NFKC, casefold, Default_Ignorable\nremoval and the UTS #39 confusable skeleton (embedded ASCII-prototype table extracted from ICU\n74.2 / Unicode 15.1, documented in track_c_fpia_workflows.py, no download). A file that is not\nvalid YAML for GitHub is FOUND (\"unparseable workflow\"); a name/stem claim is FOUND unless the\nfile is byte-identical to the authenticated R/V Track C workflow.\n\nG2 (what a complement workflow runs): YAML-decoded scalars are scanned; run steps are\ntokenised with shlex, working-directory and cd are applied, local sh/bash/python scripts,\ncomposite actions and reusable workflows (uses: ./...) are followed recursively with a cycle\nguard, and pytest selections that target Track C tests (-k/-m names, node ids, Track C test\npaths, Track C-only directories) are Track C test invocations. A whole-suite pytest run is a\nnote. result.integration_interference.dynamic_invocation_detection = NOT_CLAIMED. Without a\nYAML loader the static workflow analysis is NOT_RUN (fail-closed).\n\nG3: git fetch status lines are parsed structurally (flag \"!\", summary \"[rejected]\", reason\nfield; \"warning: rejected <ref> because ...\"; \"error:\"); a branch feature/rejected-ideas no\nlonger makes FPIA NOT_RUN.\n\nG4: an existing non-empty --out or <out>.verbatim/ is refused (FPIA_NOT_RUN, nothing written or\nrun); new --verify-output [--expect-result-sha256] rechecks result_sha256 and every side file\n(and flags unreferenced files); the CI audit step runs it (informational).\n\nG5: interpreter, site-packages, stdlib and venv paths are written as <python>,\n<site-packages>, <stdlib>, <venv> in every hashed string and side file; real values in\nrun.path_tokens. Two interpreters with identical packages at different locations give the\nidentical result_sha256 (Tier 1, two venv clones).\n\nG6: AC-04 FAIL distinguishes R_ABSENT_TRACK_C_NOT_INTEGRATED from NON_MERGE_PRESERVING_LANDING\n(status unchanged); the summary no longer prints \"NOT_RUN ()\".\n\nG7 (interpretation pending user confirmation: FPIA applies to merge results containing R): the\npull_request job runs only when the PR base or head branch matches integration/**;\nworkflow_dispatch unchanged. PyYAML==6.0.1 pinned in the install step.\n\nF2: run.authority_transport and run.canonical_ref_query record whether proxy/CA environment\nvariables were present/passed for the authority queries (names only, never values).\n\nNo change to frozen tools, Frozen records, owner/Codex branches or PR #40; no numeric threshold,\ndefault or tolerance; no PR-specific or hard-coded SHA exception.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019znshzTYgyBnuuBmSxdPFN"
    },
    {
      "id": "E014",
      "kind": "git_commit",
      "repository": "kco994553-star/Investment-System1",
      "ref": "465354a6479810a175fbefe32ef2c993b1e214c2",
      "bytes": 2608,
      "sha256": "1d40aae3b0d554326b12362d82ef5707aaf38913e3746943ecda0eb7b95ee4ca",
      "url": "https://github.com/kco994553-star/Investment-System1/commit/465354a6479810a175fbefe32ef2c993b1e214c2",
      "message": "[proposal] FPIA fix round F1-F7 (CDR-014 §7/§14): fail-closed environment, authority canonical, v2/spoof scope, verbatim streams, PR CI\n\nFixes the verified defects of dc0bf79; each has a Tier 1 regression test that fails on dc0bf79 and\npasses here. No other semantics change; no frozen tool, Frozen record or approval is touched; no\nnumeric threshold/default/tolerance and no SHA or PR literal is added.\n\nF1 Shallow or incomplete --repo: `git rev-parse --is-shallow-repository` true, any fetch that\n   refuses a ref update while exiting 0 (stderr inspected), an explicit <sha>:<ref> refspec not\n   delivered, a sandbox turned shallow, or a missing Frozen evidence head object -> NOT_RUN\n   (environment unverified), never a determinate FAIL or PASS. FROZEN_TOOLS_ON_T is NOT_RUN when\n   its canonical premise is unavailable.\nF2 The canonical ref used for FROZEN_TOOLS_ON_T is read with git ls-remote from the authority\n   remote (refs/heads/<BRANCH>); value/source in the result, query time in run metadata; never a\n   caller-local remote-tracking ref; unreachable/absent/object-less -> NOT_RUN.\nF3 v2_binding FAIL when T carries A_V-type paths while no authenticated V is an ancestor of T\n   (bytes equal or not); NOT_APPLICABLE only when T has no A_V-type path.\nF4 Frozen tools' complete stdout/stderr on T written to <out>.verbatim/ with sha256/bytes in the\n   result (work-dir path normalised as everywhere in the JSON; raw-stream sha256 in run metadata);\n   first_error no longer truncated; matched_tool_message kept.\nF5 AC-32.spoof: a generic job id collision alone is not spoofing; attribution only to R's Track C\n   workflow and V's Track C additions (V workflows carrying A_V content, byte-identical to V), not\n   V's whole tree; a workflow claiming the Track C name is never attributable.\nF6 track-c-fpia.yml: pull_request trigger (workflow_dispatch kept); subject = PR head SHA; register\n   commit = authority handoff tip via ls-remote; timeout 150 min; disk cleanup; artifact = JSON +\n   verbatim side files; job fails only via FPIA's exit code (1 FAIL, 2 NOT_RUN); status lines printed.\nF7 historical_frozen_identity.byte_protected_only lists Frozen records/CI logs that no replay\n   re-derives (with the replayed scope), also counted in the summary line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019znshzTYgyBnuuBmSxdPFN"
    },
    {
      "id": "E015",
      "kind": "git_commit",
      "repository": "kco994553-star/Investment-System1",
